  "id": "go-no-go",
  "term": "go/no-go",
  "definition": "A go/no-go task is a common psychology experiment used to measure inhibitory control. People usually make a response to frequent “go” signals, but must withhold that response to less frequent “no-go” signals, so fewer false responses on no-go trials indicate better response inhibition.",
